on/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129214/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "036da326-b309-52cc-90ba-9e5f74a4abf9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129214/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "26bc88e6-d1a5-50f9-af54-a46e3a130de5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129214/selection/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" :answer/id #uuid "e4721f9f-cad4-5384-97f4-e73d83ed8843" :answer/type