 echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "a53ef2cf-9971-5390-992b-55a335136778" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "0f23f025-8e08-5567-afcf-f28d4da09e65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "d9a2d3bd-8452-56d5-988f-e3948b7dee14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "aa1585fa-c0c0-5fe4-8c45-b063f9068672" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "2b7f2f2c-a007-5435-a6e2-7b629f233de9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d46ae25-0d83-5727-88c8-52e353847ba3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42028/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-42028/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-42028/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-42028/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-42028/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-42028/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42028" :question/id #uuid "14be2e14-3cdc-50d5-ad15-0cd8e43e35d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42028" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42028/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42028"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42006"] :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection/26b1b081859cf948d5cf4489319c7f1c5696b389cfdedbc54748d2014d24b264" :answer/id #uuid "d73fb58f-c192-57cb-8439-838be9d25723" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{33}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection/598450e2bd68f96c7aeaf149e7457caaf8ec93521689f50b3a2da3bd1a3ef220" :answer/id #uuid "ec493321-2794-5989-882d-493b0fed35c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{23}$ and ${a}_{33}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection/e224567af8fd022e0bbd6dc7a7015dd3cd82624ec22d9b9c16ccbe035186ba95" :answer/id #uuid "6cbf3228-beab-55c5-a528-66fc6f3f005b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{41}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection/642143fc9053d9d938edf2f2ca2eb5843abe23c8b800b7f91395b731b9fe7559" :answer/id #uuid "4aebc60c-61ef-5bc6-b7e0-69f7f5d2e6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{14}$ and ${a}_{41}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection/73d42bc29f5304f36e8f96a6790ce59dc1e045862a7a52d55a1263551795a538" :answer/id #uuid "c578ccc0-bbfd-55a6-8fe9-1dac9956153b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{41}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb622e6-deba-5148-8b1b-adb7aac7bf8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73154/selection/e224567af8fd022e0bbd6dc7a7015dd3cd82624ec22d9b9c16ccbe035186ba95" :answer-field/choices ["q-73154/selection/26b1b081859cf948d5cf4489319c7f1c5696b389cfdedbc54748d2014d24b264" "q-73154/selection/598450e2bd68f96c7aeaf149e7457caaf8ec93521689f50b3a2da3bd1a3ef220" "q-73154/selection/e224567af8fd022e0bbd6dc7a7015dd3cd82624ec22d9b9c16ccbe035186ba95" "q-73154/selection/642143fc9053d9d938edf2f2ca2eb5843abe23c8b800b7f91395b731b9fe7559" "q-73154/selection/73d42bc29f5304f36e8f96a6790ce59dc1e045862a7a52d55a1263551795a538"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73154" :question/id #uuid "17184586-e1d1-50c6-9cd5-9e90b02be863" :question/math-academy-id "q-73154" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{41}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73154/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73154"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection/127cb463099f3dd192d62e9b294d15a34839e817a7ce4d67d4d2bdcc61377b55" :answer/id #uuid "ae75ee24-5fb1-50a4-9612-4b988659eab1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection/26b1b081859cf948d5cf4489319c7f1c5696b389cfdedbc54748d2014d24b264" :answer/id #uuid "8280901c-241f-5458-858b-c2442bf11e5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{33}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection/35d116f468b50d221e9ed075db9f86ecc50c66be49aff5d4b41922cd89d9d79d" :answer/id #uuid "16929431-b351-5f53-8783-b9efb56c57cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{34}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection/108799ea45b4dce8f77f74c8a50ccaced6d54ff3bb86f56622d66682f47fe407" :answer/id #uuid "0e743cc4-40d5-574c-bac3-a39e05a32e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{34}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection/98c50fcc1ebb2bf9de1c7f34b6273322a9e2f7dc02207dfbd57f9fdaffd6dfac" :answer/id #uuid "35eb6d99-4b33-53f9-850f-bd9fac661115" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{43}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "782ee381-1eb8-5c6c-b0a2-c942dc08de7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42371/selection/127cb463099f3dd192d62e9b294d15a34839e817a7ce4d67d4d2bdcc61377b55" :answer-field/choices ["q-42371/selection/127cb463099f3dd192d62e9b294d15a34839e817a7ce4d67d4d2bdcc61377b55" "q-42371/selection/26b1b081859cf948d5cf4489319c7f1c5696b389cfdedbc54748d2014d24b264" "q-42371/selection/35d116f468b50d221e9ed075db9f86ecc50c66be49aff5d4b41922cd89d9d79d" "q-42371/selection/108799ea45b4dce8f77f74c8a50ccaced6d54ff3bb86f56622d66682f47fe407" "q-42371/selection/98c50fcc1ebb2bf9de1c7f34b6273322a9e2f7dc02207dfbd57f9fdaffd6dfac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42371" :question/id #uuid "ccf3269b-79b6-59e0-9353-4ad5ff8decd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42371" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6166"] :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/a29e80b35c9505ee665a109978de9b936ee7ce59eef631d7af9a4b7954bd8696.png)" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d2f89fe83787daf667e01fd4c4fe644bc36cfe23b046088c22e8de17bb02dc28.png)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4688"] :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/e300a9ac18f0170ae9053c9635fe13a9dd6def793ebfc0bd9dbe81e28810a347.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/f3d533c5687da1a75a07c6ad86b40ee8aa6ea5c86cdd250d5c47ff99b885ef61.png)\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/5d576fca72f6a4f9f0668ff0efbdc2cacc33f8dbb2c00192a7397da9ec83adea.png)\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/4f6a034def35760ae94b6eb6a425c59950556a78c124aa9ad0fcfdaa06053b28.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4687"] :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/34184a95be2b3ae6865fde109ace7e8b4397f4b01982928be73cff4199792d61.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/b9f56d3f0414f4b56b50e59c2c02d9072f1fb74ce09d801a1ab62abac61ad737.png)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/8562a693df46625ee0dc2bcdecc664dfc50a99889fdb855ae2e06dc1db02a3d4.png)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d263bfe2386309c55f1d63d97d15eaa682e9b0748a9bee6d3378d0b9035927ba.png)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/6ccb00b5e1387cd15847c50d66b26ee903d95428bcff2bfc933b675f9b590717.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4689"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/085cb01a2e4da286ea19a6f1e1707e685646af3d887abb1a57ab50e4d352c53f.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d7b93aa8abed895e49b965b8d0905088249475cad98757e7a93a174fae143b49.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
